        {
          "path": "_m/c/2/b/2/downtown-eastside-wp/homes-people-not-profi.jpg",
          "filename": "6th ANNUAL WOMEN’S HOUSING MARCH (7998506820).jpg",
          "caption": "Homes for People, not Profit for Real Estate!\nNo Slumlords, No Evictions and No Gentrification!\nRent Control not Social Control!\nHomes not Jails!\nHomes not Pipelines!\nHousing, Childcare, and Healthcare for All!\nThis year we continue to march for housing, childcare, and healthcare for all low-income residents in the DTES. We want no more evictions, no more displacement, and no more gentrification in our neighourhood. We know that the growing number of cops and condos in the DTES is part of a larger pattern to destroy and privatize neighourboods, communities, and the land. We want to live free: free from BC Housing controls, free from violence against women, and free from this system that is hurting and killing us.\n\nThe DTES Power of Women Group is a group of women (we are an inclusive group) from all walks of life who are either on social assistance, working poor, or homeless; but we are all living in extreme poverty in and around the DTES.",
          "alt": "Homes for People, not Profit for Real Estate!\nNo Slumlords, No Evictions and No Gentrification!\nRent Control not Social Control!\nHomes not Jails!\nHomes not Pipelines!\nHousing, Childcare, and Healthcare for All!\nThis year we continue to march for housing, childcare, and healthcare for all low-income residents in the DTES. We want no more evictions, no more displacement, and no more gentrification in our neighourhood. We know that the growing number of cops and condos in the DTES is part of a larger pattern to destroy and privatize neighourboods, communities, and the land. We want to live free: free from BC Housing controls, free from violence against women, and free from this system that is hurting and killing us.\n\nThe DTES Power of Women Group is a group of women (we are an inclusive group) from all walks of life who are either on social assistance, working poor, or homeless; but we are all living in extreme poverty in and around the DTES.",
          "width": 2100,
          "height": 1394,
          "mimeType": "image/jpeg",
          "license": "CC BY 2.0",
          "artist": "Caelie_Frampton from Vancouver, BC, Canada",
          "sourceUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:6th_ANNUAL_WOMEN%E2%80%99S_HOUSING_MARCH_(7998506820).jpg",
          "sourceType": "core",
